  "originalText": "For the following exercises, find the inverse of the function with the domain given.\n\n37. \\(f(x)=(x-2)^{2}, \\quad x \\geq 2\\)\n\n38. \\(f(x)=(x+4)^{2}-3, \\quad x \\geq-4\\)\n\n39. \\(f(x)=x^{2}+6 x-2, \\quad x \\geq-3\\)\n\n40. \\(f(x)=2 x^{3}-3\\)\n\n41. \\(f(x)=\\sqrt{4 x+5}-3\\)\n\n42. \\(f(x)=\\frac{x-3}{2 x+1}\\)\n\nThis page titled 5.7E: Inverses and Radical Functions (Exercises) was last modified on Thu, 26 Dec 2024 22:30:55 GMT and is shared under a CC BY  4.0  license and was authored, remixed, and/or curated by OpenStax via source content that was edited to the style and standards of the LibreTexts platform.",
